    <section style="margin-top:56px;">
        <h2 class="hf-section-title">How China treats advanced heart failure</h2>
        <p class="hf-section-sub">This is the typical sequence our partner hospitals' multidisciplinary teams (MDT) follow — first identifying the cause, then matching the right device, structural or surgical path.</p>
        <p class="hf-disclaimer" style="margin:-14px 0 24px;">Illustrative pathway — your final plan is determined by a multidisciplinary team after review of your records, not by this page.</p>
        <div class="hf-path">
            <div class="hf-step">
                <div class="hf-num">1</div>
                <span class="hf-tag">Diagnosis</span>
                <h3>Determine the cause</h3>
                <p>A multidisciplinary team reviews whether the failure is ischaemic, valvular, electrical (dyssynchrony), congenital, or from cardiomyopathy — before choosing a path.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="hf-step">
                <div class="hf-num">2</div>
                <span class="hf-tag">Device therapy</span>
                <h3>CRT · ICD · CCM</h3>
                <p>Cardiac resynchronization (CRT) re-coordinates the heartbeat, an ICD protects against sudden cardiac death, and CCM strengthens contraction when other options are exhausted.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="hf-step">
                <div class="hf-num">3</div>
                <span class="hf-tag">Structural &amp; coronary</span>
                <h3>Bypass · valve · congenital</h3>
                <p>Correcting the reversible cause — coronary bypass or stenting, valve repair or replacement (TAVR/TEER), or congenital defect repair.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="hf-step">
                <div class="hf-num">4</div>
                <span class="hf-tag">Advanced</span>
                <h3>LVAD · transplant</h3>
                <p>When the heart no longer responds, a left ventricular assist device (LVAD) or heart transplant is coordinated at a transplant center.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-top:56px;">
        <h2 class="hf-section-title">Treatment options</h2>
        <p class="hf-section-sub">The specific treatment depends on the cause your MDT identifies. Reference prices are estimates; final quotes come from the hospital after case review.</p>
        <div class="hf-treat-grid">
            <div class="hf-treat-card"><h3>CRT-P / CRT-D</h3><div class="hf-for">Resynchronizes the heartbeat for patients with LBBB or a widened QRS and reduced ejection fraction.</div><div class="hf-cost note">case-specific</div></div>
            <div class="hf-treat-card"><h3>ICD (single / dual / subcutaneous)</h3><div class="hf-for">Protects against sudden cardiac death when the risk is high.</div><div class="hf-cost note">case-specific</div></div>
            <div class="hf-treat-card"><h3>CCM</h3><div class="hf-for">Cardiac contractility modulation to strengthen contraction when standard device therapy is not suitable.</div><div class="hf-cost note">case-specific</div></div>
            <div class="hf-treat-card"><h3>Coronary stenting / CABG</h3><div class="hf-for">Restores blood flow for ischemic (blocked-artery) heart failure.</div><div class="hf-cost">$12,000–$18,000</div></div>
            <div class="hf-treat-card"><h3>Valve repair / replacement (TAVR/TEER)</h3><div class="hf-for">Corrects severe mitral or aortic valve disease, including minimally invasive options.</div><div class="hf-cost">$10,000–$15,000</div></div>
            <div class="hf-treat-card"><h3>LVAD</h3><div class="hf-for">A left ventricular assist device supports the heart when other treatments are exhausted.</div><div class="hf-cost note">case-specific</div></div>
            <div class="hf-treat-card"><h3>Heart transplant</h3><div class="hf-for">For end-stage heart failure, coordinated at a transplant center.</div><div class="hf-cost note">case-specific</div></div>
        </div>
    </section>

